.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VFS_SYNC 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vfs_sync
.Nd flush dirty buffers to disk
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/mount.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vfs_sync "struct mount *mp" "int waitfor" "struct ucred *cred" "struct thread *td"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vfs_sync
function flushes dirty buffers associated with the filesystem
.Fa mp
to disk.
If
.Fa mp
is NULL, all mounted filesystems are synced.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa waitfor"
.It Fa mp
The filesystem to sync, or NULL for all.
.It Fa waitfor
If MNT_WAIT, the function waits for I/O completion.
If MNT_NOWAIT, it initiates I/O but does not wait.
.It Fa cred
Credentials to use for the operation.
.It Fa td
The thread performing the operation.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfs_mount 9 ,
.Xr sync 2
